From: NotProtonNot <332734261+NotProtonNot@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: A copy-on-write view of a page-file section is mapped writable and shared outside Linux; 2XKO's copy protection needs it. From NotProton's creator

Patch by NotProton's creator (https://github.com/NotProtonNot/NotProton), handed to
MacGameFix. Only the file name changed here; the diff is theirs as given.

--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
@@ -3232,6 +3232,12 @@
     if (res) goto done;
 
     TRACE( "handle=%p size=%lx offset=%s\n", handle, size, wine_dbgstr_longlong(offset.QuadPart) );
+#ifndef __linux__
+    if (!(sec_flags & SEC_FILE) && (vprot & VPROT_WRITECOPY))
+        res = map_file_into_view( view, unix_handle, 0, size, offset.QuadPart,
+                                  (vprot & ~VPROT_WRITECOPY) | VPROT_WRITE, needs_close );
+    else
+#endif
     res = map_file_into_view( view, unix_handle, 0, size, offset.QuadPart, vprot, needs_close );
     if (res == STATUS_SUCCESS)
     {
